[statement]
apk takes a name's candidates in turn, keeping the better of each pair,
and two versions of one package go by version where other candidates tie:
`c` 1, `d` 1 and `c` 2 provide `w` at 3, `d` 1 ties with `c` 1, and `c` 2
outranks `c` 1, so apk installs `c` 2. Listed `d` 1 first, `d` 1 is kept
against both, and apk installs it
(`of-two-versions-providing-a-name-alike-the-later-is-chosen-in-turn-another-first`).

[repository]
P:c
V:1
p:w=3

P:d
V:1
p:w=3

P:c
V:2
p:w=3

[request]
w

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install c 2
